From d65a11d17917148a6081e04338d6d215e48602c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 21:07:14 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 167/174] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali-oneplus-iceland: fix the
 WCN7860 PMU supplies

The WCN7860 power sequencer takes VDD_IO_1P2, VDD_ANT, VDD_AON,
VDD_DIG, VDD_RFA_1P8, VDD_RFA_1P2 and VDD_CX. The node still used the
WCN7850 names: it described a vddio supply that the WCN7860 sequencer
never requests, fed VDD_AON from S1J and had no VDD_CX, so the boot log
showed "supply vddcx not found, using dummy regulator" and Linux never
voted for L2G.

Wire the inputs as the vendor tree of this tablet does: VDD_AON from
L2G (1.8 V) and VDD_CX from S1J, and drop the unused vddio supply. The
board has no antenna-share supply, so VDD_ANT stays undescribed.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
index 23d085e87..ccae84bf9 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
@@ -466,12 +466,16 @@ wcn7860-pmu {
 		wlan-enable-gpios = <&tlmm 16 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 		bt-enable-gpios = <&pmh0104_j_e1_gpios 5 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 
-		vddio-supply = <&vreg_l2g_1p8>;
+		/*
+		 * As stock's Wi-Fi node: AON from L2G (1.8 V), CX from S1J; the
+		 * board has no antenna-share supply (vddant).
+		 */
 		vddio1p2-supply = <&vreg_l3g_1p2>;
-		vddaon-supply = <&vreg_s1j_0p8>;
+		vddaon-supply = <&vreg_l2g_1p8>;
 		vdddig-supply = <&vreg_s2j_0p8>;
 		vddrfa1p2-supply = <&vreg_s7f_1p2>;
 		vddrfa1p8-supply = <&vreg_s8f_1p8>;
+		vddcx-supply = <&vreg_s1j_0p8>;
 
 		clocks = <&rpmhcc RPMH_RF_CLK1>;
 
